	abstract = {We study a generalization due to De Gregorio and Wunsch et.al. of the Constantin-Lax-Majda equation (gCLM) on the real line {\textbackslash}[ ω\_t + a u ω\_x = u\_x ω- νΛ{\textasciicircum}γ ω, {\textbackslash}quad u\_x = H ω, {\textbackslash}] where \$H\$ is the Hilbert transform and \$Λ= (-{\textbackslash}partial\_\{xx\}){\textasciicircum}\{1/2\}\$. We use the method in {\textbackslash}cite\{chen2019finite\} to prove finite time self-similar blowup for \$a\$ close to \${\textbackslash}frac\{1\}\{2\}\$ and \$γ=2\$ by establishing nonlinear stability of an approximate self-similar profile. For \$a{\textgreater}-1\$, we discuss several classes of initial data and establish global well-posedness and an one-point blowup criterion for different initial data. For \$a{\textbackslash}leq-1\$, we prove global well-posedness for gCLM with critical and supercritical dissipation.},
